--
--   Description
--
-- This test checks the transmit functionality for gigabit burst mode. Also, 
-- this test verifies that the GEM will not transmit more than the maximum burst
-- limit (64K bits per burst).
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- · Ensures the proper implementation for the transmission of frame bursts.
-- · Ensures that the transmit functionality of the GEM can break in and out 
--   of frame bursts. (i.e. The GEM can transmit a frame burst. Then, transmit 
--   a normal sized frame. Finally, re-start transmission of a new frame burst.) 
-- · Ensures that the GEM will not transmit more than the burst limit of 64K 
--   bits per burst.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- Transmit Functionality in Burst Mode:
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for gigabit operation.
-- 2. In burst mode, transmit a frame with minimum frame size plus extension. 
--      Then, transmit two minimum sized frames.  
-- 3. In normal mode, transmit a frame with minimum frame size plus extension.
-- 4. In burst mode, transmit a frame with minimum frame size plus extension. 
--      Then, transmit two minimum sized frames.  
-- 5. In normal mode, transmit a frame with minimum frame size plus extension.
-- 6. Check status registers and statistic registers and ensure that the above 
--      operations did not result in any errors.
-- Burst Limit:
-- 7. In burst mode, 
--      transmit five maximum sized frames (1518 bytes)
--      transmit a frame with 482 bytes
--      transmit a minimum sized frame (64 bytes)
--      This should cause the GEM burst timer to expire just at the point
--      where the 64 byte frame is about to start being transmitted
--      (just after the IPG). Therefore all frames will appear as one burst.
-- 8. In burst mode, 
--      transmit five maximum sized frames (1518 bytes)
--      transmit a frame with 483 bytes
--      transmit a minimum sized frame (64 bytes)
--      This should cause the GEM burst timer to expire one byte before the 
--      final 64 byte frame is about to start being transmitted (just before 
--      the end of the IPG). 
--      The result should be that the first five 1518 byte frames and the 483
--      byte frame are transmitted as a burst, but the final 64 byte frame
--      is transmitted as a single frame with carrier extension. The final
--      IPG between the 483 byte frame and the 64 byte frame shall be signalled
--      as idle.
-- 9. Check status registers and statistic registers and ensure that the above 
--      operations did not result in any errors.
-- 
-- Note:  The burst counter includes all framing bits and inter-frame gap (IFG)
--        between each frame in it's frame burst limit calculation.
--
-- The test for burst limit has the following breakdown in bytes:
--     1st frame   8 byte preamble & SFD
--                 1518 bytes
--                 12 bytes (IFG)
--     2nd frame   8 byte preamble & SFD
--                 1518 bytes
--                 12 bytes (IFG)
--     3rd frame   8 byte preamble & SFD
--                 1518 bytes
--                 12 bytes (IFG)
--     4th frame   8 byte preamble & SFD
--                 1518 bytes
--                 12 bytes (IFG)
--     5th frame   8 byte preamble & SFD
--                 1518 bytes
--                 12 bytes (IFG)
--     6th frame   8 byte preamble & SFD
--                 482 bytes or 483 bytes
--                 12 bytes (IFG) ****LAST FRAME OF BURST****
--  
--     (burst counter should reach burst limit of 8192 bytes)
-- 
--     7th frame   8 byte preamble & SFD
--                 64 bytes
--                 plus extension           This last frame should be
--                                          transmitted in burst mode for
--                                          test 7 and non-burst mode for
--                                          test 8 (i.e. the frame should 
--                                          be transmitted with 64 bytes
--                                          plus extension).
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


